  "issue_number": 181,
  "issue_title": "[bug] Math scorer does not unwrap \\mathbf/\\boldsymbol (unlike \\text/\\mathrm), so \\mathbf{5} scores wrong vs 5",
  "issue_body": "**Describe the bug**\n\n`normalize_math_answer` (`src/trinity/orchestration/reward.py`) unwraps two LaTeX font commands to their content:\n\n```python\ns = re.sub(r\"\\\\text\\s*\\{([^{}]*)\\}\", r\"\\1\", s)\ns = re.sub(r\"\\\\mathrm\\s*\\{([^{}]*)\\}\", r\"\\1\", s)\n```\n\nbut not the other common font/style wrappers \u2014 `\\mathbf`, `\\boldsymbol`, `\\mathit`, `\\mathsf`, `\\mathtt`. These change only how an answer *looks*, not its value, yet a wrapped answer is left with the raw command and scores 0. Confirmed (reference `\"5\"`, benchmark `math500`):\n\n```python\nscore_text(\"math500\", r\"\\boxed{\\text{5}}\",   \"5\")  # -> 1.0  (\\text is unwrapped)\nscore_text(\"math500\", r\"\\boxed{\\mathbf{5}}\", \"5\")  # -> 0.0  (\\mathbf is not; should be 1.0)\nnormalize_math_answer(r\"\\mathbf{5}\")               # -> '\\\\mathbf{5}'  (should be '5')\n```\n\nSo a model that bolds its final answer (`\\boxed{\\mathbf{5}}`) is graded wrong while an identical `\\text{5}` is graded right.\n\n**Expected vs actual**\n\n- *Expected:* all pure font/style wrappers unwrap to their content, so `\\mathbf{5}` normalizes to `5` just like `\\text{5}`/`\\mathrm{5}`.\n- *Actual:* only `\\text` and `\\mathrm` are unwrapped; `\\mathbf`, `\\boldsymbol`, `\\mathit`, `\\mathsf`, `\\mathtt` survive and cause false negatives.\n\n**To reproduce**\n\n```python\nfrom trinity.orchestration.reward import normalize_math_answer, score_text\nprint(score_text(\"math500\", r\"\\boxed{\\mathbf{5}}\", \"5\"))  # 0.0, should be 1.0\nprint(normalize_math_answer(r\"\\boldsymbol{42}\"))          # '\\\\boldsymbol{42}', should be '42'\n```\n\n**Environment**\n- Python version: 3.10+\n- GPU: CPU only (pure/offline math scorer, no torch)\n- Commit hash: current `main` (`c23c767`)\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T04:09:36.000Z",
